  "mean": "“Am” is a helper word: it links the person doing something to what they are, do or did, as in “I am awake.”",
  "know": "Your child needs to recognise “am” at a glance, say it clearly, and begin to hear it in the stories you read together. Good hunting grounds: morning routines: “I am hungry”, “I am ready”, “I am here”.",
  "why": "Helper words like “am” cannot be drawn as a simple picture, so they are best learned by seeing them again and again in sentences.",
  "dev": "Sentence sense, letter-sound matching on irregular spellings and fluent reading of short sentences.",
