  "say": "Look at this card. It says ‘am’. I am awake. Now you say ‘am’. Well done!",
  "teach": "1) Show the card and read “am” clearly, running your finger under the letters. Let your child say it back, twice.\n2) Look at the picture together: a boy sits up in bed, stretching his arms beside a sunny window. Ask what is happening, then link the picture to the word.\n3) Play one tiny game: wake up slowly from a pretend sleep and announce “I am awake!”. Read the word one last time and stop while it is still fun.",
  "notice": "Point to the word first, then to the picture. Cover the picture with your hand and read the word; lift your hand to check. Then let your child trace the first letter with one finger.",
  "ask": "“What does the card say?” “Can you say it in a sentence?” “Who is doing something in the picture?” — answered with a read-aloud and a short sentence of their own.",
  "childSay": "Expect your child to read “am” aloud before sounding it out, and to use it in everyday sentences like “I am awake.”",
  "real": "Watch for “am” here: morning routines: “I am hungry”, “I am ready”, “I am here”. Every sighting is a free practice round: point, say it, move on.",
